-- title:
--   Two generators modulo 𝔪 from a balanced involution
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m =$ `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R`, and suppose $2$ is a unit in $R$. Let $V$ be an $R$-module and let $\tau \colon V \to V$ be an $R$-linear map which is an involution, in the sense that the composite $\tau \circ \tau$ is the identity map. Let $X, Y \subseteq V$ be submodules that are complementary ($X \cap Y = 0$ and $X + Y = V$), with $X$ isomorphic as an $R$-module to $R$ itself, and with $Y$ indecomposable in the sense that whenever two submodules $W_1, W_2$ of $Y$ are complementary, at least one of them is zero. Assume further that the images of the two eigen-submodules $\ker(\tau - \mathrm{id})$ and $\ker(\tau + \mathrm{id})$ under the quotient map $V \to V/\mathfrak m V$ (where $\mathfrak m V$ is $\mathfrak m \cdot \top$) are isomorphic as $R$-modules. The conclusion is that there exist $v, w \in V$ with $R v + R w + \mathfrak m V = V$, i.e. $V$ is generated by two elements modulo $\mathfrak m V$; the asserted $v, w$ are not required to be related to $\tau$, $X$ or $Y$.
--
--   This is the module-theoretic core of the Krull–Schmidt argument of Tilouine and of Mazur–Wiles, used by Wiles in the proof of multiplicity one at an ordinary, $p$-distinguished maximal ideal: a module which is the sum of a free rank-one piece and an indecomposable piece, carrying an involution whose two eigen-pieces have equal residual dimension, needs only two generators modulo the maximal ideal. It is invoked in the construction of two generators for the corner submodule of the relevant $H^1$ in the ordinary, absolutely irreducible case.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_exists_span_pair_sup_maximalIdeal_smul_top_eq_top_of_isCompl_of_involution.lean

